// shacc: precise
// NativeRes: fragment program for nativeres_texture_v.cg: wide copies of
// off-screen targets (wide_targets.rs, DESIGN "sixty-sixth session").
//
// Drawn into an 8888 surface twice as wide as the copied part of the
// target: pixel 2x of a row gets texel x's (r, r, g, g), pixel 2x + 1 its
// (b, b, a, a). Those bytes are one U16x4 texel holding k x 257 in each
// channel (read back as k / 255), the texture the GE_WIDE programs filter
// exactly (texture cache GpuFormat::Wide16). The quad maps two pixels onto
// each texel, so the point-filtered read lands a quarter texel off its
// centre; the pixel's column parity comes from its window position (pixel
// centre or corner: either way the fraction of x / 2 is below 0.5 only for
// even columns). Each channel written exactly as read (8-bit out).
//
// Compiled on the Vita with the shader compiler app (README.md "Shaders").

float4 main(
	float2 vTexcoord : TEXCOORD0,
	float4 vPosition : WPOS,
	uniform sampler2D tex) : COLOR
{
	float4 texel = tex2D<float4>(tex, vTexcoord);
	return frac(vPosition.x * 0.5f) < 0.5f ? texel.xxyy : texel.zzww;
}
